  "title": "bmm and baddbmm perf regression on CPU",
  "issue_id": "162553",
  "bug_description": "As called out by @jainapurva, https://github.com/pytorch/pytorch/actions/workflows/operator_benchmark.yml reports a significant regression on the following 2 ops on CPU:\n* `bmm_B128_M64_N32_K64_cpu_dtypetorch.bfloat16`\n* `baddbmm_B128_M64_N32_K64_cpu_dtypetorch.bfloat16`\n\nThis workflow was added by Intel for CPU a while ago, and there is interest from the team to expand this to cover `torch.compile` and CUDA too, i.e. https://github.com/pytorch/pytorch/pull/161394.\n\nWe should look into these regressions, and decide if they need to be fixed.  And if yes, before or after 2.9 release.  In the longer term, if op_benchmark workflow is proven useful, we need to find a proper owner to monitor it\n\ncc @jerryzh168 @jgong5 @mingfeima @XiaobingSuper @sanchitintel @ashokei @jingxu10 @jainapurva @atalman @malfet",
